								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=219"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:shyranphyton@hotmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1073.msg10551#msg10551"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1073.msg10551#msg10551">Re: Conviction</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #21 on:</b> August 27, 2004, 04:50:38 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Llew is not back&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/dissappointed.gif" alt="dissappointed" border="0" /><br />not yet at least.<br /><br />I really don&#039;t understand where the &quot;anti-conviction&quot; sentiment stems from...I see the guild chat, group with my teammates and have a great time raiding..I have no clue who would lack the tact to recruit this way.&nbsp; If we had names, we might be able to make the connection, but I honestly don&#039;t know anyone in my guild that would do something like this.... <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cwm1.gif" alt="cwm1" border="0" /><br /><br />If there are some Conviction guildies who are out dragging our name through the mud..PLEASE do us a favor and send someone a DIRECT tell asking for an officer.&nbsp; <br /><br />Like the other day, when some guy called from Playboy and asked me to be Playmate of the year, and get the modeling contract, free car, cash, clothes, etc....and I didn&#039;t write his name and number down before my cell phone lost signal...but really it did happen!
						</td>
